= The Military Prosecutors Turn Against the CHP

The trial of TÖS has become politically sensitive due to the indictment prepared by six prosecutors from the Ankara Martial Law Command. Apart from allegations concerning the activities of the teachers' union, these prosecutors have included very serious accusations against the CHP and İsmet İnönü. The indictment accuses the party of having pursued misguided policies after the death of Atatürk, mismanaging the economy, interfering in the events following May 27, and failing to uphold the principles of the Republic. However, it is particularly alarming that such accusations have been made by military prosecutors who are supposed to administer justice impartially on behalf of the state.

Among the accusations attributed to the prosecutors are:

{! <ul><li>İnönü and the Left of Center movement have deliberately attempted to legitimize communism in Turkey.</li><li>The CHP's leadership and members have engaged in widespread corruption and pursued their personal interests at the country's expense.</li><li>İnönü's administration was responsible for the economic stagnation and difficulties experienced during World War II, rather than the war itself.</li><li>İnönü deliberately divided the MBK following May 27 and interfered with its objectives for his own political benefit.</li><li>The CHP deliberately undermined Turkey's political and economic development during its coalition governments between 1961 and 1965.</li><li>The CHP has encouraged communist ideas and engaged in communist propaganda.</li><li>The CHP has sheltered members of Dev-Genç within its ranks, while Dev-Genç has allegedly carried out activities on behalf of the party.</li><li>The CHP established the Village Institutes as a means of spreading communism and political unrest throughout the country.</li></ul> !}

İnönü becomes extremely furious at the accusations and considers them an attempt to besmirch him and his party. After guiding Turkey through the perils of World War II and overseeing its transition to multiparty democracy, he finds it unacceptable that military prosecutors are now portraying him as a traitor. İnönü, Atatürk's right-hand man, the man who won our first military victory in the War of Independence, our chief Prime Minister during Atatürk's presidency, the very same man who consistently placed the safety of democracy above the interests of himself and his party, just so our Republic could flourish, is now being slandered and potentially threatened by the fascist junta!

İnönü claims that the accusations are entirely politically motivated and have no place in an indictment concerning the activities of a teachers' union. He questions what authority the military prosecutors believe they have to pass judgment on decades of Turkish political history. Under İnönü's leadership, the executive committees of the CHP's parliamentary groups and the Central Executive Committee issue a joint statement condemning the accusations and calling on the government to take responsibility for the actions of the military prosecutors. He makes it clear that although he holds the Turkish Armed Forces in high regard, he cannot accept these attacks on his party and the democratic institutions of Turkey...

- @post_event: This conflict is only just beginning.
